:: Breakfast [simulation activity] {"position":"1400,650","size":"100,100"}
<h1>Breakfast Time</h1>\
<hr>\
<<if State.variables.myRole == "patient">>\
It's time for breakfast. What would you like to have for breakfast today @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@? As you think about what to have you try to figure out which option will give you the most energy for your errands today.
<hr>
<<patient-choices "Breakfast choices" "no-eval"
	"A 24-ounce high protein smoothie and a 20-ounce cup of coffee | -2 | warm | red | Too much liquid all at once makes you feel really full and makes it harder to breathe | | Points+=1"
    "An 8-ounce cup of coffee, cottage cheese with fruit | 1 | warm | green | Just the right amount of food and liquid in one meal is easier for you to eat. You feel refreshed and plan to pack a protein bar as a snack for later | | Points+=1"
	"An 8-ounce cup of coffee, a glass of orange juice, two slices of toast, two fried eggs, two turkey sausage links and an apple | -2 | warm | red | It was delicious, but your body can't handle eating the way you did as a teenager anymore. All that food and liquid was filling and made it harder to breathe | | Points+=1"
>>\

<<patient-next "Time to run errands" "Hallway_Out">>\

<<else>>\

@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ is going to pick what he wants for breakfast. Here are his options this morning. Which do you think he'll choose? What will give him the most energy for the busy day ahead?
<hr>
<ul>
<li>A 24-ounce high protein smoothie and a 20-ounce cup of coffee</li>
<li>An 8-ounce cup of coffee, cottage cheese with fruit</li>
<li>An 8-ounce cup of coffee, a glass of orange juice, two slices of toast, two fried eggs, two turkey sausage links and an apple</li>
</ul>
//There are no activity specific evaluations for this station//
<</if>>

<!--[[Hallway_Out]]-->


:: Dressing [simulation activity] {"position":"1600,650","size":"100,100"}
<h1>Getting Dressed</h1>\
<hr>\
<<if State.variables.myRole == "patient">>\
Time to get dressed for the day. <strong>Make sure to put on your socks and shoes</strong> so you can run your errands.
<hr>
<<patient-next "Time for breakfast!" "Breakfast">>\

<<else>>\

It's time for @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ to get dressed. Once they are done getting dressed evaluate their performance below.
//Don't forget that you can use your general controls as well to add or subtract additional energy such as if they bend over to put their shoes on//
<hr>
<<dynamic-eval "Activity: Getting Dressed"
" They got dressed sitting down | -1 | 1 | satAndRested | green | You're dressed and ready for breakfast | green"
"They got dressed standing up | -3 | 1 | standing | red | Even putting your clothes on for the day makes you feel winded, you wonder if you'll be able to do all your errands today | red"
>>

<</if>>

<!--[[Breakfast]]-->


:: Errands_Hub [simulation] {"position":"2800,1100","size":"100,100"}
<h1>Whistle Stop Park</h1>\
<hr>\
<<if $myRole == "patient">>\
You're at Whistle Stop Park. Choose an errand below, or head home when you are done for the day.

<<silently>>
<<set _errandGroceryClass to "eval-wrap errands-cell green-wrap">>
<<if $visitedGrocery>><<set _errandGroceryClass to "eval-wrap errands-cell errands-cell--visited">><</if>>
<<set _errandPharmacyClass to "eval-wrap errands-cell green-wrap">>
<<if $visitedPharmacy>><<set _errandPharmacyClass to "eval-wrap errands-cell errands-cell--visited">><</if>>
<<set _errandClinicClass to "eval-wrap errands-cell green-wrap">>
<<if $visitedClinic>><<set _errandClinicClass to "eval-wrap errands-cell errands-cell--visited">><</if>>
<<set _errandToyClass to "eval-wrap errands-cell green-wrap">>
<<if $visitedToyStore>><<set _errandToyClass to "eval-wrap errands-cell errands-cell--visited">><</if>>
<</silently>>

<div class="errands-hub">
<div class="errands-grid">\
<span class="<<print _errandGroceryClass>>">\
<<if $visitedGrocery>>\
<button type="button" class="errands-btn" disabled>🛒 Grocery Store ✓</button>\
<<else>>\
<<button "🛒 Grocery Store">><<run SimApp.nextPassage("Grocery_Store_Router")>><</button>>\
<</if>>\
</span><span class="<<print _errandPharmacyClass>>">\
<<if $visitedPharmacy>>\
<button type="button" class="errands-btn" disabled>💊 Pharmacy ✓</button>\
<<else>>\
<<button "💊 Pharmacy">><<run SimApp.nextPassage("Pharmacy_Router")>><</button>>\
<</if>>\
</span><span class="<<print _errandClinicClass>>">\
<<if $visitedClinic>>\
<button type="button" class="errands-btn" disabled>🩺 Pulmonary Clinic ✓</button>\
<<else>>\
<<button "🩺 Pulmonary Clinic">><<run SimApp.nextPassage("Pulmonary_Clinic")>><</button>>\
<</if>>\
</span><span class="<<print _errandToyClass>>">\
<<if $visitedToyStore>>\
<button type="button" class="errands-btn" disabled>🧸 Toy Store ✓</button>\
<<else>>\
<<button "🧸 Toy Store">><<run SimApp.nextPassage("Toy_Store_Router")>><</button>>\
<</if>>\
</span>\
</div>
  <div class="errands-hub__footer">
    <span class="eval-wrap blue-wrap errands-hub__done">
      <<button "🏠 Done for the day. Head back home">>
        <<run SimApp.nextPassage("Whistle_Stop_In")>>
      <</button>>
    </span>
  </div>
</div>

<<else>>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ is at Whistle Stop Park. He may visit the grocery store, pharmacy, pulmonary clinic, or toy store. Use your general observation controls in the footer as he moves and completes each errand.
<</if>>


:: Grocery_Store_Router [simulation activity] {"position":"2900,1000","size":"100,100"}
/* One shared roll (server-side on Cloudflare), then both players go to the same passage */
<<run SimApp.routeByRoll("groceryRoll", ["Grocery_Store_1", "Grocery_Store_2"], "visitedGrocery")>>

<!--[[Grocery_Store_1]]-->
<!--[[Grocery_Store_2]]-->
:: Grocery_Store_1 [simulation activity] {"position":"2900,1000","size":"100,100"}
<h1>Grocery Store</h1>\
<hr>\
<<if $myRole == "patient">>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@, you arrive at the grocery store to pick up a few essentials for the week.

The parking lot is completely packed. You walk inside, but all of the motorized shopping carts are already in use. You have no choice but to grab a standard cart and push it through the crowded aisles yourself.

<<patient-choices "What do you want to do?" "no-eval"
  "Grab a regular shopping cart | -4 | blue | red | Pushing the heavy cart and dodging crowds is exhausting. | | Points+=1 | standing+=1 | errandsRun+=1"
  "It's too much work without a motorized cart. You'll come back tomorrow | 0 | blue | red | Hopefully you'll be able to find a motorized cart tomorrow. | | Points-=1"
>>\

<<patient-next "Head back to the park" "Errands_Hub">>\

<<else>>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ is at the grocery store, but the parking lot is completely packed. Heading inside he discovers that all of the motorized shopping carts are already in use. He now has to decide if he wants to push the cart through the crowded aisles or if he'll come back tomorrow.

<</if>>

:: Grocery_Store_2 [simulation activity] {"position":"2900,1000","size":"100,100"}
<h1>Grocery Store</h1>\
<hr>\
<<if $myRole == "patient">>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@, you arrive at the grocery store to pick up a few essentials for the week.

The store is surprisingly quiet today. Right inside the door, there is a fully charged motorized shopping cart waiting for you! You sit down and comfortably glide through the aisles to gather your groceries.
<<patient-choices "Time to shop" "no-eval"
  "Grab the motorized cart | -1 | green | green | Using the motorized cart saves you a lot of energy | | Points+=1 | errandsRun+=1"
>>\

<<patient-next "Head back to the park" "Errands_Hub">>\

<<else>>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ is at the grocery store and the store is surprisingly quiet today. Heading inside he discovers that there is a fully charged motorized shopping cart waiting for him!

<</if>>

