:: Toy_Store_1 [simulation activity] {"position":"3100,1200","size":"100,100"}
<h1>Toy Store</h1>\
<hr>\
<<if $myRole == "patient">>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@, you are at the toy store to pick up a gift for your granddaughter.

The store is in total chaos with a weekend sale! To make matters worse, the specific doll she asked for is on the very bottom shelf at the back of the store.

<<patient-choices "Look for a doll" "no-eval"
  "Pick up the doll | -4 | blue | red | Bending down and navigating the chaotic store severely depletes your energy. But you're happy you got your granddaughter the doll she wanted. | | Points+=4 | bentOver+=1 | hasToy=true | errandsRun+=1"
>>

<<patient-next "Head back to the park" "Errands_Hub">>\

<<else>>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ is at the toy store to pick up a gift for his granddaughter. The store is in total chaos with a weekend sale! To make matters worse, the specific doll she asked for is on the very bottom shelf at the back of the store.
Observe his pacing and breathing using your general observation controls.
<</if>>

:: Toy_Store_2 [simulation activity] {"position":"3100,1200","size":"100,100"}
<h1>Toy Store</h1>\
<hr>\
<<if $myRole == "patient">>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@, you are at the toy store to pick up a gift for your granddaughter. As soon as you walk in, a friendly clerk greets you. They see that you might have a hard time navigating the aisles packed with kids for a weekend sale. When you mention the doll you are looking for, they offer to fetch it from the back room and bring it directly to the front register for you. You are able to wait comfortably near the entrance.


<<patient-choices "Purchase the doll" "no-eval"
  "Purchase the doll | -1 | blue | green | Asking for assistance prevents unnecessary exertion and keeps your breathing steady. You feel slightly embarrassed asking for help, but you're glad you got your granddaughter her birthday present | | Points+=4 | hasToy=true | errandsRun+=1"
>>

<<patient-next "Head back to the park" "Errands_Hub">>\

<<else>>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ is at the toy store to pick up a gift for his granddaughter. The store is in total chaos with a weekend sale! But a friendly clerk has offered to fetch the doll for @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ while he waits comfortably near the entrance.
Observe his pacing and breathing using your general observation controls.
<</if>>

:: Whistle_Stop_In [simulation activity] {"position":"2700,1100","size":"100,100"}
<<silently>>
/* Energy -= errandsRun², once per visit (server-side on Cloudflare) */
<<run SimApp.applyErrandsDrain()>>
<</silently>>
<h1>Heading back</h1>\
<hr>\
<<if $myRole == "patient">>\
You wrap up your errands at Whistle Stop Park and prepare to head back to your apartment. 

As you stand there, the cumulative physical toll of the day's activities suddenly hits you. <<if $errandsRun >= 2>>Pushing through $errandsRun errands in one day has severely drained your reserves.<</if>><<if $errandsRun == 1>>Even one errand has taken a toll on you.<</if>><<if $errandsRun < 1>>Even just the walk to the park has taken a toll on you.<</if>>

<<patient-choices "Before you head home" "no-eval"
  "You sit down to rest for a moment | +1 | blue | green | You're exhausted and need a break. You sit down and rest for a moment before heading home. | | satAndRested+=1"
  "You push through the exhaustion and continue on | -4 | blue | red | You're determined to get home. You push through the exhaustion and keep walking. | | rushed+=1"
>>

<<patient-next "Walk back to your apartment" "Hallway_In">>

<<else>>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ is heading home from Whistle Stop Park. Observe his pacing and breathing using your general observation controls as he heads home.
<</if>>


:: Hallway_In [simulation activity] {"position":"2600,700","size":"100,100"}
<h1>Walking back to your apartment</h1>\
<hr>\
<<if $myRole == "patient">>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@, go ahead and walk back up to your apartment.

<<patient-next "Time for Dinner" "Dinner">>\

<<else>>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ is heading back up to his apartment. Evaluate how he moves through the building.

<<dynamic-eval "Activity: Walking up stairs"
"They took the elevator | -1 | 1 | elevator | green | Taking the elevator makes it a lot easier | green"
"They took the stairs | -9 | 1 | stairs | red | You can't believe you made it up all those stairs. It felt like climbing a mountain! | red"
>>

<</if>>

:: Dinner [simulation activity] {"position":"2600,700","size":"100,100"}
<h1>Dinnertime</h1>\
<hr>\
<<if $myRole == "patient">>\
Evening has come, and your thoughts turn towards dinner. You could either order yourself a pizza or cook your own meal.

<<patient-choices "Dinner choices" "no-eval"
  "Order a pizza | -1 | blue | red | The food is a little greasy and heavy, and you feel a little guilty spending the extra money instead of cooking. But you feel tired after a long day. And you can't deny that pizza tastes great!| | Points-=3"
  "Cook your own meal | -3 | blue | red | After a long day cooking is exhausting. You hope you have enough energy left over to get you to bed. || Points+=1"
>>

<<patient-next "One last chore" "Laundry">>\

<<else>>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ is in his apartment and it's time to eat dinner. He has to decide between ordering pizza or cooking his own meal.
<</if>>

:: Laundry [simulation activity] {"position":"2600,700","size":"100,100"}
<h1>Laundry</h1>\
<hr>\
<<if $myRole == "patient">>\
You make your way to the laundry area. The clothes are clean, but they are sitting in a heavy basket on the floor waiting to be folded. You are already feeling the exhaustion of the day settling deep into your chest.

<<patient-choices "Laundry choices" "no-eval"
  "Fold the clothes | -2 | green | red | You decide to push through the fatigue and fold the laundry. | Laundry_Fold"
  "Leave the laundry for tomorrow | 0 | red | red | You decide to leave the laundry in the basket. It's frustrating to let chores pile up, but your body is begging for rest tonight. | Bedtime"
>>

<<patient-next "Continue" "Bedtime">>

<<else>>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ is back in his apartment and it's time to do laundry. Watch what he decides — if he skips folding, there is no activity-specific eval at this station.
<</if>>

:: Laundry_Fold [simulation activity] {"position":"2600,750","size":"100,100"}
<h1>Folding Laundry</h1>\
<hr>\
<<if $myRole == "patient">>\
You push through the fatigue and begin folding the clothes in the basket.

<<patient-next "Time for bed" "Bedtime">>

<<else>>\
@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ is folding laundry. Evaluate whether he sits or stands while folding.

<<dynamic-eval "Activity: Folding laundry"
  "They folded the clothes sitting down | -1 | 2 | satAndRested | green | You pushed through the fatigue to get the laundry folded. | green"
  "They folded the clothes standing up | -3 | 0 | standing | red | The constant bending over to pull clothes out of the basket takes a toll on your breath. | red"
>>
<</if>>

:: Bedtime [simulation activity pausetimer recap nobr] {"position":"2600,700","size":"100,100"}
<h1>Bedtime</h1>
<hr>
<<if $myRole == "patient">>
You finally make it to your bedroom and sit on the edge of the mattress.
    <<if $Energy <= 3>>
    You're utterly exhausted and feel like you can barely breathe, but you made it.
    <<elseif $Energy <= 7>>
    You're a little winded, and glad to be done for the day.
    <<else>>
    You're feeling good and looking forward to a good night's sleep.
    <</if>>
    <<if $hasMedications is true>>
    You change into your pajamas and set your medications on the night stand for tomorrow morning.
    <<else>>
    As you change into your pajamas you worry about how you'll feel tomorrow without your maintenance medications.
    <</if>>
    You crawl into bed and lay your head on the pillow and close your eyes. As you drift off to sleep you
    <<if $hasToy is true>>
    think about how excited your granddaughter is going to be when you give her the doll you bought...
    <<else>>
    feel guilty about not having a present for your granddaughter's birthday tomorrow...
    <</if>>
<<patient-next "Finish the day and view your final report" "Final_Report">>
<<else>>
    @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ is back in his bedroom. As he gets ready for bed he reflects on how his breathing is feeling and what he was able to get done today.
    <<if $Energy <= 3>>
    He is utterly exhausted and feels like he can barely breathe, but he made it.
    <<elseif $Energy <= 7>>
    He is a little winded, and glad to be done for the day.
    <<else>>
    He is feeling good and looking forward to a good night's sleep.
    <</if>>
    <<if $hasMedications is true>>
    He changes into his pajamas and sets his medications on the night stand for tomorrow morning.
    <<else>>
    As he changes into his pajamas he worries about how he'll feel tomorrow without his maintenance medications.
    <</if>>
    He crawls into bed and lays his head on the pillow and closes his eyes. As he drifts off to sleep he
    <<if $hasToy is true>>
    thinks about how excited his granddaughter is going to be when he gives her the doll he bought...
    <<else>>
    feels guilty about not having a present for his granddaughter's birthday tomorrow...
    <</if>>
<</if>>

:: Final_Report [simulation briefing hidehud recap nobr] {"position":"2600,800","size":"100,100"}
<<silently>>
<<audio ":playing" stop>>
<<run SimApp.prepareFinalReport()>>
<<set _elapsed to SimApp.getElapsedParts()>>
<<set _minutes to _elapsed.totalMinutes>>
<<set _seconds to _elapsed.seconds>>
<<if _seconds < 10>>
<<set _secondsPad to "0" + _seconds>>
<<else>>
<<set _secondsPad to "" + _seconds>>
<</if>>
<</silently>>
<div style="text-align:center;">
<h1>Simulation Complete</h1>
<<if SimApp.getTeamName()>><h3>Team <<print SimApp.getTeamName()>></h3><</if>>
<<if $win is true>>
<h2>@@color:green;Mr. Holland made it through the day safely.@@</h2>
<<else>>
<h2>@@color:red;Mr. Holland ended up in the hospital.@@</h2>
<</if>>
</div>
<hr>
<h3>Final Results:</h3>
<ul style="margin-top:0; padding-top:0;">
<li>''Time Elapsed:'' <<print _minutes>>:<<print _secondsPad>></li>
<li>''Remaining Energy:'' $Energy / 15</li>
<li>''Total Points Earned:'' $Points</li>
<li>''Rescue Inhaler Uses:'' $Inhaler / 6</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3>Energy Debrief</h3>
<<if $win is true>>
@@color:green;Conservation Technique Stats:@@
<ul style="margin-top:0; padding-top:0;">
<li>''Pursed Lip Breathing:'' Used $pursedLip times (Recovered $pursedLipTotal Energy)</li>
<li>''Sitting & Resting:'' Used $satAndRested times (Recovered $restingTotal Energy)</li>
<li>''Total Energy Recaptured:'' $totalRecovered points.</li>
</ul>
    <<if $Inhaler >= 4>>
    @@color:red;Needs Improvement:@@ You relied heavily on the rescue inhaler today. While it is there for emergencies, needing it this frequently indicates that Mr. Holland was pushed past his safe exertion limits. Next time, try to use more energy-conservation techniques!
    <<elseif $Energy <= 3>>
    @@color:yellow;Borderline:@@ You completed the day, but Mr. Holland is completely exhausted. You successfully avoided overusing the inhaler, but managing his pacing earlier in the day would have left him with a safer energy reserve.
    <<else>>
    @@color:green;Excellent Work:@@ You perfectly balanced Mr. Holland's daily errands with his energy limits. You used energy-conservation techniques effectively and kept his breathing stable without over-relying on his rescue medication!
    <</if>>
<<else>>
    <<if $Energy is 0>>
    @@color:red;Mr. Holland is in the hospital:@@ You overexerted yourself today. Here is the breakdown of the physical demands of your day:
    <<elseif $Inhaler >= 7>>
    @@color:red;Mr. Holland is in the hospital:@@ You used your inhaler $Inhaler times. Using your inhaler too much increases your risk of tachycardic dysrhythmias due to albuterol's impact on beta-1 adrenergic receptors. Relying on the rescue inhaler instead of energy conservation techniques increases your risk for adverse medication reactions. Here is a breakdown of the physical demands of your day:
    <<else>>
    @@color:red;Mr. Holland is in the hospital:@@ Here is a breakdown of the physical demands of your day:
    <</if>>

    <ul style="margin-top:0; padding-top:0;">
    <<if $errandsRun >= 1>>
    <li>''Errands Completed:'' $errandsRun (Exertion cost: $errandsDrain energy). Running multiple errands in one day takes an increasing toll on your limited energy reserves.</li>
    <</if>>
    <li>''Stair Climbs:'' $stairs (Taking the stairs, even once, can cause severe shortness of breath.)</li>
    <li>''Bending Over:'' $bentOver (Every time you bend over, you constrict your lungs and make it harder to breathe.)</li>
    <li>''Times Rushed:'' $rushed (Rushing through tasks will make you winded quickly.)</li>
    <li>''Tasks Completed Standing:'' $standing (Standing up while completing activities of daily living or errands is fatiguing. When possible, complete tasks sitting down to conserve energy.)</li>
    </ul>
<</if>>

<<if $wildCarded is true>>
<h3>Wild Card Debrief:</h3>
<<if $wildRoll is 1>>
<h4 class="wild-card-event">Event: Forgot Inhaler</h4>
<br>
Realizing you forgot your rescue inhaler could have had devastating consequences. You either had to expend more energy to go back upstairs to your apartment or risk going all day without it. Going without your inhaler leaves you reliant on pacing yourself and using good breathing techniques to manage your energy, but you are only one trigger away from needing an ambulance!
<<elseif $wildRoll is 2>>
<h4 class="wild-card-event">Event: Caved to a Craving</h4>
<br>
Nicotine addiction is a powerful hurdle. Smoking that cigarette caused immediate airway irritation and dropped Mr. Holland's energy. Managing chronic illness isn't about being perfect, it's about handling setbacks and continuing to try.
<<elseif $wildRoll is 3>>
<h4 class="wild-card-event">Event: Wildfire Smoke</h4>
<br>
The heavy particulate matter from the wildfire smoke made the air dangerous to breathe today. Navigating severe environmental hazards requires protecting your airway, strict energy conservation, and recognizing when it is too dangerous to push forward.
<<elseif $wildRoll is 4>>
<h4 class="wild-card-event">Event: Freezing Cold Air</h4>
<br>
Cold, dry air is a major trigger for bronchospasms in COPD patients. Managing this sudden shock to the lungs meant pacing yourself carefully and taking extra time to recover after the exposure.
<<elseif $wildRoll is 5>>
<h4 class="wild-card-event">Event: Beautiful Day</h4>
<br>
Living with a chronic illness is incredibly taxing on mental health. Having a beautiful, clear day provided a much-needed morale boost, reminding you of the little things in life that make the daily struggle worth it!
<<elseif $wildRoll is 6>>
<h4 class="wild-card-event">Event: Heavy Pollen</h4>
<br>
The blooming trees filled the air with allergens, triggering airway inflammation. You had to carefully manage this extra respiratory burden while just trying to get through a normal daily routine.
<</if>>
<</if>>

<hr>
<br><br>
<div style="text-align:center;">
@@color:green;Great job! Please show this screen to your instructor.@@
</div>
<div style="text-align:center;">
<<link "Try Again?">><<run SimApp.restartFromDebrief()>><</link>>
</div>

