:: Simulation_Hub [simulation briefing nobr] {"position":"1200,450","size":"100,100"}
<h1>Tutorial & Controls Practice</h1>
<<if State.variables.myRole == "patient">>
<h2>Welcome to the game @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@</h2>
<hr>
This is what your user interface will look like when you start the game. At the top of your screen you will see your heads up display <strong>HUD</strong>, showing:
<ul>
<li>The time elapsed in the simulation.</li>
<li>Your current work of breathing.</li>
<li>Whether you have your rescue inhaler with you.</li>
</ul>

The clock is running now so you can see the real <strong>HUD</strong> in action. It will reset to zero when you start the actual simulation.

If you have your rescue inhaler with you, during the simulation you may demonstrate correct inhaler technique to your @@.observer;Observer@@ and they will add some energy. Don't forget to keep track of how many times you have used it during the simulation. You can only use it <strong>6 times per day</strong> according to the doctor.

For now, use the <strong><u>Practice Activity</u></strong> button at the bottom of your screen to try a sample action and see how it impacts your work of breathing.
<hr>
    <<patient-next "Begin Practice Activity" "Tutorial_Jumping_Jacks" "reset">>
<<else>>
<h2>Welcome to the game @@.observer;Observer@@!</h2>
<hr>
You will be following along with @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ and assessing how well he conserves his energy as he goes about his day. 
This is what your user interface will look like when you start the game. At the top of your screen you will see your heads up display, <strong>HUD</strong> showing:
<ul>
<li>The time elapsed in the simulation. //Don't worry about the clock ticking right now it will reset after these tutorial pages when we start the actual simulation//</li>
<li>@@.holland;Mr. Holland's@@ current energy</li>
<li>If @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ has his inhaler</li>
<li>How many points he has earned</li>
</ul>

The clock is running now so you can see the real HUD in action. It will reset to zero when you start the actual simulation.

<h3>How the Simulation Works</h3>
* ''Hidden Stats:'' The student playing @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ cannot see their exact energy or inhaler uses. They will only see a rough estimate of their breathing status.
* ''Gaining Energy:'' They can use energy-conserving techniques to regain energy.
* ''Inhaler Use:'' They can use their albuterol rescue inhaler to regain energy, but make sure your partner actually demonstrates correct technique for it to count.
* ''Losing Energy:'' They will lose energy if they rush, don't take breaks, or bend over (which compresses their lungs and makes it harder to breathe).
* ''Button Limits:'' The assessment buttons in the footer can only be used once per activity, but they will reset at the next station.

<h3>Practice Area</h3>
Try clicking the buttons at the bottom of the screen in ''General Observations'' right now to see how they affect @@.holland;Mr. Holland's@@ energy level!

For some activities, you will be provided with different options that automatically assign points and energy based on how @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ performed.

Once you feel comfortable with the controls and @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ is comfortable with the practice activities, they will start the simulation from their screen.
<</if>>

<!--[[Tutorial_Jumping_Jacks]]-->


:: Start [nobr]{"position":"800,400","size":"200,200"}
<<run if (window.SimApp) { SimApp.revealConnectButton(); }>>
<div class="center-heading1">@@.holland;Mr Holland's@@ Grand Day Out</div>
<div class="center-heading3">Version <<print Story.title.replace(/^COPD simulation\s+/i, "")>></div>
<hr>
<div class="center-heading2">An interactive augmented reality simulation by Robin Parker, MSN, RN, PCCN</div>
<div class="center-heading3">Cursor AI was used to assist with coding and debugging</div>
Welcome to this live augmented reality nursing simulation. You will need a partner to complete this activity. 
Before we begin please review the briefing below, then follow the steps under <strong>To start the game</strong> at the bottom of this page.
<hr>
<h2>Briefing</h2>
<p>Today you and your partner will be living a day in the life of @@.holland;Mr. Bernard Holland@@, a 75-year-old retired carpet layer who is living with COPD. He is a 60-pack-year smoker who is currently trying to quit. He does not wear home oxygen, though he does often have to stop to catch his breath after walking for more than a few minutes on level ground.</p>

<h3>Home Medications</h3>
Mr. Holland is prescribed multiple medications to help him manage his COPD including twice daily maintenance inhalers along with an oral maintenance bronchodilator. In addition to his maintenance medications he has also been prescribed a <strong>rescue inhaler</strong> to use when he is experiencing a sudden increase in his symptoms.
<h3>Simulation Goals</h3>   
<ul>
<li>Your goal  is to accomplish as many tasks during your day as possible. This is a <strong>timed simulation</strong>. You and your partner will be competing against your classmates!</li>
<li>Each activity your team completes will earn you points, with some activities being worth more points than others.</li>
<li>At the end of the simulation the winning team will be determined by the amount of points earned during the simulation. In the event of a tie, the fastest time will be used to break the tie.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Roles</h3>
<ul>
<li>@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@: In this role you will be making choices about what activities to complete and how to perform those activities to conserve your energy. </li>
<li>@@.observer;The Observer@@:  In this role you will be evaluating  @@.holland;Mr. Holland's@@ performance throughout his daily routine. You will be adding and deducting energy based on how your partner acts out the activities.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Augmented Reality Approach</h3>
<ul>
<li>To give you an understanding of what it is like to live with a chronic illness, the student playing the role of  @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ will need to act out many of the activities as if you are actually doing them. For example putting on your shoes will require actually putting on your shoes, while folding laundry will require you to fold a pile of laundry.</li>
<li>@@.observer;The Observer@@ will assign energy additions or subtractions based on @@.holland;Mr. Holland's@@ actual physical performance of that task.</li>
<li>Once you connect to the multiplayer lobby the student playing the role of @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ will be controlling the pace of the game and moving from activity station to activity station. The game will tell you where to go next or it may give you options to choose from.</li>
<li>Meanwhile, @@.observer;the Observer@@ will be provided specific scoring buttons for each task.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Energy Management</h3>
<ul>
<li>@@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ will start with @@color:green;10 energy@@ and can have a maximum of @@color:green;15 energy@@.</li>
<li>Each task you perform will cost energy, with certain tasks or choices costing more than others. </li>
<li>When you use energy conservation techniques or use your rescue inhaler @@.observer;The Observer@@ will be able to @@color:green; add energy@@. Conversely not using good breathing technique can result in @@color:red; subtracting energy@@</li>
<li>If @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ reaches @@color:red; 0 energy@@, it's game over and you will have to return to <strong>room 8220 for debriefing.</strong></li>
</ul>

<h3>Today's Itinerary</h3>
The game will start with  @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ getting out of bed in the morning, which will start the clock for the simulation. After that, you’ll need to shower, brush your teeth, get dressed, along with other activities of daily living.
<br>
It’s coming up on the end of the month and @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ has a lot of errands on his to-do list including:
<ul>
<li>Go to the grocery store.</li>
<li>Pick up his prescriptions <strong>(He is almost out of his maintenance medications, fortunately he still has an extra rescue inhaler!)</strong>.</li>
<li>An appointment at the pulmonary rehab clinic.</li>
<li>Go to the toy store to buy a gift for his granddaughter's 7th birthday tomorrow.</li>
</ul>

<h2>To start the game</h2>
<ol>
<li>One member from each team scans the QR code below. This will create your team.</li>
<li>Invite your partner to join. Have your partner scan the new QR code on your device.</li>
<li>Choose your roles. One of you will play the role of @@.holland;Mr. Holland@@ while the other will be @@.observer;the Observer@@.</li>
<li>After you have chosen your roles, follow the instructions on the screen.</li>
</ol>
<div id="loading-overlay">Loading multiplayer services...</div>
<div id="connect-container" class="hidden">
    <<button "Connect to Multiplayer">>
        <<run SimApp.connect()>>
    <</button>>
</div>

<!--[[Role_Selection]]-->
<!--[[Waiting_Room]]-->


:: StoryCaption {"position":"300,400","size":"100,100"}
<<if $devmode && State.variables.myRole == "patient">>
	<<run UIBar.show()>>
<h2>Dev Mode</h2>\

<details>
    <summary><strong>Score & Status</strong></summary>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="Energy">Energy: <<numberbox "$Energy" $Energy>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="Points">Points: <<numberbox "$Points" $Points>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="Inhaler">Inhaler Uses: <<numberbox "$Inhaler" $Inhaler>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="win">Win State:
    <<listbox "$win" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
   </details>

   <details>
    <summary><strong>Techniques</strong></summary>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="satAndRested">Sat/Rested: <<numberbox "$satAndRested" $satAndRested>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="pursedLip">Pursed Lip: <<numberbox "$pursedLip" $pursedLip>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="rushed">Rushed: <<numberbox "$rushed" $rushed>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="bentOver">Bent Over: <<numberbox "$bentOver" $bentOver>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="stairs">Stairs: <<numberbox "$stairs" $stairs>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="elevator">Elevator: <<numberbox "$elevator" $elevator>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="standing">Standing: <<numberbox "$standing" $standing>></span>
   </details>

  <details>
    <summary><strong>Locations & Events</strong></summary>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="errandsRun">Errands Run: <<numberbox "$errandsRun" $errandsRun>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="wildRoll">Wild Roll: <<numberbox "$wildRoll" $wildRoll>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="wildCarded">Wild Carded:
    <<listbox "$wildCarded" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="visitedHallway">Visited Hallway:
    <<listbox "$visitedHallway" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="visitedGrocery">Visited Grocery:
    <<listbox "$visitedGrocery" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="visitedPharmacy">Visited Pharmacy:
    <<listbox "$visitedPharmacy" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="visitedToyStore">Visited Toy Store:
    <<listbox "$visitedToyStore" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="visitedClinic">Visited Clinic:
    <<listbox "$visitedClinic" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
   </details>

 <details>
    <summary><strong>Inventory</strong></summary>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="yourItem">Your Item: <<textbox "$yourItem" $yourItem>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="hisItem">His Item: <<textbox "$hisItem" $hisItem>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="hasInhaler">Has Inhaler:
    <<listbox "$hasInhaler" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="hasMedications">Has Meds:
    <<listbox "$hasMedications" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
    <span class="dev-var" data-dev-key="hasToy">Has Toy:
    <<listbox "$hasToy" autoselect>>
        <<option "true" true>>
        <<option "false" false>>
    <</listbox>></span>
 </details>

    ---
//**Passage Navigator**//
    Passage Name:
    <<textbox "_jumpTarget" "">>
    <<button "Jump To Passage (team)">>
        <<if Story.has(_jumpTarget)>>
            <<run SimApp.goToSharedPassage(_jumpTarget)>>
        <<else>>
            <<run UI.alert("Error: Passage '" + _jumpTarget + "' does not exist.")>>
        <</if>>
    <</button>>

    <<button "Sync from Playroom">>
        <<run SimApp.syncFromPlayroom(); SimApp.refreshDevCaptionUI(); SimApp.updateHud()>>
    <</button>>
    ---
<<script>>
setTimeout(function () {
    if (window.SimApp && State.variables.devmode) {
        SimApp.wireDevCaptionControls();
    }
}, Engine.minDomActionDelay);
<</script>>
<</if>>


:: StoryInit {"position":"700,200","size":"100,100"}
<<script>>
(function () {
    var vp = document.querySelector('meta[name="viewport"]');
    if (vp) {
        vp.setAttribute("content", "width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover");
    }
})();
<</script>>
<<run UIBar.hide()>>
<<set $devmode to false>>
/* Multiplayer / role fallbacks (offline testing) */
<<set $myRole to "">>
<<set $evalComplete to false>>
<<set $patientFeedback to "">>
<<set $patientFeedbackColor to "">>

/* Score Keeping Fallbacks */
<<set $Energy to 10>>
<<set $Points to 0>>
<<set $Inhaler to 0>>
<<set $win to false>>

/* Energy Conservation Technique Fallbacks */
<<set $satAndRested to 0>>
<<set $pursedLip to 0>>
<<set $rushed to 0>>
<<set $bentOver to 0>>
<<set $stairs to 0>>
<<set $elevator to 0>>
<<set $standing to 0>>

/* Visited Fallbacks */
<<set $wildCarded to false>>
<<set $wildRoll to 1>>
<<set $groceryRoll to 1>>
<<set $pharmacyRoll to 1>>
<<set $toyStoreRoll to 1>>
<<set $yourItem to "">>
<<set $hisItem to "">>
<<set $visitedHallway to false>>
<<set $visitedGrocery to false>>
<<set $visitedPharmacy to false>>
<<set $visitedToyStore to false>>
<<set $visitedClinic to false>>
<<set $errandsRun to 0>>

/* Inventory Fallbacks */
<<set $hasInhaler to true>>
<<set $hasMedications to false>>
<<set $hasToy to false>>

